# Allow-list: only what the build reads enters the context.
# Anything else that lands in the working tree, such as a .env, a dump or a
# stale generated specification, stays out without an entry of its own; a file
# the build needs and this list omits fails the build loudly.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!Makefile
# The Makefile reads it when parsed, so make prints an error without it.
!.golangci-lint-version
!cmd/
!internal/
!migrations/
# Only the embed file: the image generates its own specification.
!docs/embed.go

# Tests are not built; leaving them out also keeps a test edit from
# invalidating the build cache.
**/*_test.go
